From c496fb4fd80dab4c2c2036e5acabb543e1feed5e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tesseract XRT port <jwkim@limagin.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 11:11:50 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 05/19] xocl: drop .llseek = no_llseek on Linux 6.12+

Since mainline commit 868941b14441 ("fs: remove no_llseek", v6.0)
no_llseek has been "#define no_llseek NULL", and a NULL ->llseek makes
do_dentry_open() clear FMODE_LSEEK so lseek() returns -ESPIPE. Commit
cb787f4ac0c2 ("[tree-wide] finally take no_llseek out", v6.12) then
removed the macro, so the trace debugfs fops in xocl_debug.c no longer
compile.

Guard: LINUX_VERSION_CODE < KERNEL_VERSION(6, 12, 0) keeps the
initializer (checked: mainline v6.11 <linux/fs.h> still defines it,
v6.12 does not).

Equivalence: exact. On 6.0..6.11 the initializer already stored NULL;
on 6.12+ the field is left NULL by omission.

Upstream: same hunk as XRT commit 04350f685.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01SpY5QiU1d7kAe8YJM35EvA
---
 driver/xocl/xocl_debug.c | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/driver/xocl/xocl_debug.c b/driver/xocl/xocl_debug.c
index 194b5b2..43d049a 100644
--- a/driver/xocl/xocl_debug.c
+++ b/driver/xocl/xocl_debug.c
@@ -145,7 +145,9 @@ static const struct file_operations trace_fops = {
 	.open = trace_open,
 	.release = trace_release,
 	.read = trace_read,
+#if LINUX_VERSION_CODE < KERNEL_VERSION(6, 12, 0)
 	.llseek = no_llseek,
+#endif
 };
 
 static ssize_t trace_mod_read(struct file *file, char __user *buf,
